sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Acanthometra pellucida Schnakenberg wavelength at 206 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 81.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Analytical lambda_c at gamma 10 is 206.0 nm by the length-unit choice. Nonlinear FFT peaks track lambda_c(gamma) with Pearson r = 0.9991 and RMSE = 43.30 nm (the peaks sit systematically long). Equal diffusion drops std(u) by a factor of about 2300. The first drawing, with spines through the disk, had specimen-image radial-profile r = 0.548, orientation KS = 0.113, and cv_sim_similarity = 90.2 on a 12-frame 960x680 GIF. Eight dark-edge axes were detected against Müller's 20. Weighted score 81.5. These render numbers are the pre-remediation run. The measurement sidecar is generated from the checkpoint script, which already contains the pass-2 edits, so the sidecar reports radial r = 0.096, held-out RMSE = 6.09 nm, and cv is not stored there. v2 is the score of that checkpoint script. Overall 81.5/100 (faithfulness 80.1, reproducibility 84.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit f1fee7075fcbec51969593b452b4632c61bd2928; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 78, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py at f1fee7075fcbec51969593b452b4632c61bd2928, image/png, 688006 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 f35dc4b0b74fce257c0fa2cc609f91bf704de3e79d1d0e29c093724b48f66fd4 (sha256 f35dc4b0b74fce257c0fa2cc609f91bf704de3e79d1d0e29c093724b48f66fd4), spec_fingerprint e39627dd2e1ab0061d44983f5e20e147e309799aaead4a87c95c97412dce57d6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e39627dd2e1ab0061d44983f5e20e147e309799aaead4a87c95c97412dce57d6; artifact_sha256: f35dc4b0b74fce257c0fa2cc609f91bf704de3e79d1d0e29c093724b48f66fd4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0/acanthometra_pellucida_specimen.jpg=f07186d3f18203f0..., datasets/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=879c1b1d04423021...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) reaction-diffusion and a critical wavelength; Gierer and Meinhardt (1972) activator-inhibitor kinetics; Murray (1981) the critical-wavenumber formula used for prepatterns. | Haeckel (1904) Kunstformen der Natur, Tafel 21, is a published drawing captioned Acanthometra. | Decelle et al. (2012) describe living acantharians. They do not report a 206 nm pigment period.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian at (a, b) = (0.14, 0.76), k_c^2 = (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv), and a six-point gamma sweep on a periodic 96x96 patch. | Equal-diffusion ablation. Spine-axis angles measured on the vendored plate crop.; transfer_boundary: 206 nm (2.064e-7 m, log10 -6.685) is the assigned detail scale. The length unit is chosen so the analytical wavelength equals that number. The plate's scale is the printed drawing, not 206 nm. | Chronoseries 1/1 at 0 Ma. There is no fossil predecessor in this slot. The comparison is with a 412 nm octave on a 1339 nm patch (6 waves versus 3).; does_not_claim: That celestite spicules of A. pellucida have been shown to form by this Schnakenberg system. | That Tafel 21 figure 2 is a photograph of the type of A. pellucida. | That the plate resolves a 206 nm carrier.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1. The 43.30 nm RMSE is a systematic long shift. Estimate one scale on gamma 4, 7, 10 and score gamma 14, 19, 26.",
            "remediation needed: R2. Add an autocatalysis knockout (no u^2 v) besides equal diffusion.",
            "remediation needed: R3. Leave the 206 nm carrier visible on the capsule instead of covering the disk with crossing spines." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.815"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single builder-assessor; no second provider scored this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

